// endpoint_set_workspace_correspondence.proto — SetWorkspaceCorrespondence:
// mark a workspace as AWAITING CORRESPONDENCE from another workspace, or clear
// the mark. AGENT API section.
//
// A WORKSPACE WAITING ON ANOTHER IS NOT IDLE. An agent that asked another
// workspace for something and ends its turn to wait for the answer marks
// itself awaiting that workspace; when the answer arrives it clears the mark.
// While the mark stands and no turn runs, every surface draws the workspace
// in the BACKGROUND status, as one whose detached work is still running
// (frontend.v1.FooterStatusBackground.awaiting), so the user can tell a
// workspace that is waiting on purpose from one that is done.
//
// THE MARK IS THE AGENT'S TO CLEAR: the daemon cannot judge whether a reply
// is the one awaited. It ends on its own only when the workspace closes, or
// when the awaited workspace is forgotten.
//
// Independent of the one-shot mark (SetWorkspaceOneShot).

